<title>MEXICO: Mexico stocks continue bull charge.</title>
<headline>Mexico stocks continue bull charge.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican stocks continued to outstrip previous record gains in early afternoon trading on Thursday.</p>
<p>Dealers said both foreign and local bulls scrambled to buy as surplus liquidity released by lower U.S. long bond yields took refuge in Mexican equities.</p>
<p>The leading IPC share index had soared 150.09 points, or 3.02 percent, at 5,124.32.</p>
<p>(( --Martin Roberts, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7907))</p>
